{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug reporting back — root cause proven, fix pushed (Gerrit 2323)\n\n**Problem.** On a `--ref A`-targeted completion verification the verifier's\nprefetch injected LIVE-checkout (B) file bodies into its verdict-bearing\n`<prefetched_file_contents>` evidence, instead of the `--ref`-pinned code\nsnapshot (A). This violates the ticket's public contract: checks that judge\nthe implementation must use the `--ref` code revision; live-checkout content\nmust never become verdict evidence for a `--ref`-targeted run.\n\n**Proven root cause.** `gate_ops.completion_precheck` calls\n`completion_prefetch.assemble_prefetch(spec, repo_root=ctx.repo_root)`, where\n`ctx.repo_root` is the LIVE checkout / ticket-store root the workflow threads\nthrough — deliberately (ticket reads need it). But `assemble_prefetch` also\nperformed the *verdict-bearing WORKING-TREE reads* — `_read_body(repo_root, …)`\nfor declared `file_impact` bodies and `_discover_test_globs(repo_root, …)` —\nfrom that same live `repo_root`, never consulting the pinned snapshot the\nattested gate had activated via `use_code_root(handle.path)` /\n`current_code_root()`. Every OTHER verdict-bearing read already pins A (agent\ntools via `cfg.repo_path`/`use_code_root`; reconcile citations at\n`gate_ops.py:290`; the signed `verified_at_sha` = `handle.sha`). Prefetch was\nthe sole leak.\n\n**Proof (runtime).** Built a real attested gate context\n(`gate_source.gate_read_root(SnapshotHandle(path=snap_A, sha=…,\nsource=SOURCE_ATTESTED))`) with a divergent A/B fixture (live B and pinned A\ndeclare the same path with different bytes). Asserted the gate really pinned A\n(`current_code_root() == snap_A`), then called the real\n`assemble_prefetch(repo_root=live_B)`. Before fix: section contained\n`LIVE_B_CONTENT`, not `PINNED_A_CONTENT` → leak confirmed. After fix: section\ncontains A, not B.\n\n**Defect origin + caused_by.** Introduced by commit `6d343d13626c` (ticket\n`a9dd-bbc7-f549-4fc2`, \"prefetch file_impact into verifier context\"). At that\ncommit's parent, `resolve_code_root`/`use_code_root` already existed, so this\nis an unmet-obligation / incomplete-implementation (the new prefetch reads did\nnot honor the pinned-code-root contract that pre-existed them), not a carrier\nregression. Recorded `caused_by → a9dd-bbc7-f549-4fc2`.\n\n**Test path.**\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch_pinned_root_831f.py` — held-out\noracle driving the real `gate_read_root` + `assemble_prefetch` path with the\nA/B fixture; asserts the prefetch section carries A, not B, under an attested\ngate (RED before fix), plus a negative control asserting local/no-gate mode\nstill reads the passed `repo_root`. Offline: stubs only `_reads.show_ticket`.\n\n**Fix.** `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_prefetch.py`: re-root ONLY the\nworking-tree reads to\n`code_root = resolve_code_root(allow_checkout_fallback=False) or repo_root`\n(yields the active snapshot A under a gate; falls back to `repo_root` in\nlocal/no-gate mode, preserving behavior). `_discover_test_globs` and\n`_read_body` now use `code_root`. Ticket reads (`show_ticket`,\n`_subtree_impacts`) and immutable-by-SHA `referencing_commit_diffs` stay on\n`repo_root` (the materialized snapshot has no `.git`; a commit diff is fixed by\nits SHA, not live state). Import goes through `rebar.llm.config` per the\ngate_context seam contract.\n\n**Scope & safety.** Localized, behavior-preserving. Local/no-gate mode\nunchanged (no active snapshot → `resolve_code_root` returns None → falls back\nto `repo_root`). No CLI/schema/API/output-contract surface change. Sole\nreal-content caller is `gate_ops.completion_precheck`; `operations.assemble_context`\npasses `prefetch=None` on all code-review paths (sibling-parity checked).\n`make lint` (ruff + complexity + module-size) and `make typecheck` pass; the\nexisting 26-test prefetch suite + gate_context seam suite pass.\n\n**Siblings swept.** (1) Other verdict-bearing code reads passing live\n`repo_root` where the snapshot should win — reconcile citations and agent\ntools already pin A (no leak). (2) Parity: the code-review gate prefetch path —\n`assemble_context(prefetch=None)` on every review caller, so no analogous leak.\nNo sibling tickets required.\n\n**Residual risk.** Low. The only behavioral change is under an active attested\nsnapshot gate, which is exactly the `--ref` path the contract governs. Immutable\ncommit-diff reads intentionally remain on the live object store (content-addressed\nby SHA).\n\n**Replication.** The held-out test is the end-to-end reproduction (real gate +\nreal prefetch, divergent A/B). Mutation-checked (re-seeding the exact defect\nturns the test RED).\n\n**Disposition:** FIX pushed to Gerrit change 2323\n(https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2323). Awaiting `LLM-Review +1`\nand `Verified +1`; will Submit and close `--class=plan_defect\n--caused-by=a9dd-bbc7-f549-4fc2` once both are green and merged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787939008215193001,"uuid":"a97b2a72-cdf7-4043-80cc-6e34cb06fd4a"}